@host = http://localhost:5080

### Small talk -> tier 1 -> cheapest capable: lmstudio-small
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "hello, how are you today?" } ]
}

### Simple coding task -> tier 2 + "code" capability -> lmstudio-coder
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "write a unit test for this function: int Add(int a, int b) => a + b;" } ]
}

### Architecture question -> tier 4 -> claude-code (subscription, marginal cost 0)
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Compare the trade-offs between event sourcing and a CRUD data model for our billing system." } ]
}

### Matches a tier-1 route, but complexity raises it (structure + reasoning keywords)
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Summarize this article in three bullet points, then analyze the implications step by step and evaluate the trade-offs:\n1. Revenue grew 12%\n2. Churn doubled\n3. Two competitors merged\nWhat does this mean for us? What should we do next?" } ]
}

### Sensitive data -> LocalOnly route -> only local models, even on failover
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Look up the customer record for account number 4471" } ]
}

### Per-request strategy: the most capable model available
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto:best",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "hello" } ]
}

### Force a specific catalog model
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "lmstudio-coder",
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "explain closures in JavaScript" } ]
}

### Streaming (Dispatch mode streams real tokens from LM Studio or the Claude CLI)
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "auto",
  "stream": true,
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "tell me a joke" } ]
}

### Models and aliases (shows cooldowns after a subscription hits its limit)
GET {{host}}/v1/models

### Diagnostics: tier, reason, route scores and the ranked models, without calling any model
POST {{host}}/semantic-router/classify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "prompt": "why does this async code deadlock when I call .Result?" }


### Anthropic Messages API (what Claude Code sends when ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points here)
POST {{host}}/v1/messages
Content-Type: application/json
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01

{
  "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5",
  "max_tokens": 256,
  "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "Compare event sourcing and CRUD for a billing system." } ]
}

### Anthropic token count (no model is called)
POST {{host}}/v1/messages/count_tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{ "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5", "messages": [ { "role": "user", "content": "hello there" } ] }

### Dashboard status (admin API; loopback only)
GET {{host}}/router/api/status
